You had burger and fries?

49
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,160
Yeah, maybe.

50
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:03,240
Well, it's not very healthy and there's a great way to describe this.

51
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:04,180
The word is unhealthy.

52
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:07,680
Alright, so yes, as you say, it's very unhealthy.

53
00:02:07,980 --> 00:02:09,500
Well, yeah, because you get fat.

54
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:10,780
They're very high in calories.

55
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,260
So it's unhealthy.

56
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:13,760
So that means it's not good for you.

57
00:02:13,980 --> 00:02:14,340
That's right.

58
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:23,840
So just a reminder, in English, when we hear the word unhealthy or unhappy, this means not healthy, not happy.

59
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,980
Un is a prefix that means not.

60
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:31,440
Okay, and talking about unhealthy food, in general, what are we talking about?

61
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:32,860
We're talking about fast food.

62
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:37,080
Okay, so this might require a story.

63
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:40,380
What is the meaning behind fast food as opposed to slow food?

64
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:41,920
Because there is no slow food, right?

65
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,340
I think now they have it in like France or something like that.

66
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:47,360
They talk about slow food.

67
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:50,120
But anyways, fast food is food that is prepared very quickly.

68
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:54,780
So you go, you order, in two or three minutes, you have your entire order ready to go.

69
00:02:55,240 --> 00:03:06,650
Okay, so maybe this is the food that I could get at McDonald's or Burger King where they make it very, very quickly and I can go home or I can go to the office with my food ready.

70
00:03:06,950 --> 00:03:07,330
Exactly.

71
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:18,480
So fast food, very popular among countries, very popular nowadays among busy people who have no time to sit down at a restaurant or eat or sit down and have a proper lunch.

72
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:18,730
Fast food.

73
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:25,070
And one of the important drinks at a fast food restaurant is a carbonated drink.

74
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:27,730
So this carbonated, what does this mean?

75
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:32,310
This is actually the fancy word for soda or for fizzy drink.

76
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:33,580
Fizzy, okay.

77
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:36,120
So something that's carbonated has bubbles.

78
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:37,340
Yeah, it has bubbles.

79
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:40,620
For example, a lot of Europeans drink carbonated water.

80
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:43,520
That means water with bubbles in it.

81
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:43,680
That's right.

82
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:50,670
So actually, the bubbles are caused because the drink has a high concentration of a certain gas such as carbon.

83
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:54,970
So that's why it has all these bubbles and it's fizzy like Coca-Cola for example.

84
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:58,050
Right, Coca-Cola or Sprite, these are carbonated drinks.

85
00:03:58,640 --> 00:03:59,640
Very good.

86
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:01,470
So you have carbonated water and you have carbonated soda.

87
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:04,510
What is the thing that makes soda different?

88
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,490
What is it that makes soda taste so good?

89
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,710
It's sweet and the ingredient that makes it sweet is called fructose syrup.

90
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,710
Fructose syrup is essentially sugar.

91
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:18,150
Yeah, and it comes from corn I believe, right?

92
00:04:18,230 --> 00:04:18,550
That's right.

93
00:04:18,790 --> 00:04:29,550
So you can also hear the name corn syrup and this is a sweet syrup that comes from corn that makes drinks like Sprite and Coca-Cola taste so good.

94
00:04:30,150 --> 00:04:31,830
It's also very unhealthy for you.

95
00:04:31,970 --> 00:04:34,230
Yes, because it has a lot of calories.

96
00:04:34,710 --> 00:04:37,530
So that is one of the main ingredients in soda.

97
00:04:37,830 --> 00:04:40,010
Now you know you have fructose syrup.

98
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,100
