125
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:45,480
This is a very interesting phrase because we saw it in the first sentence and it says, let's go grab a bite to eat.

126
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:46,980
Let's grab a bite to eat.

127
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:52,220
So to grab is to hold something with your hand, okay, to do it quickly.

128
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,100
He grabbed my arm.

129
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:58,120
So to grab a bite to eat, a bite is a small taste.

130
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:01,100
We're going to have a quick meal.

131
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:04,130
So after work, you want to go grab a bite to eat?

132
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:06,960
That means let's go have something to eat quickly.

133
00:06:07,030 --> 00:06:08,210
Yeah, I'll be there soon.

134
00:06:08,430 --> 00:06:09,750
Let me just grab a bite to eat.

135
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,800
So bite is a little bit.

136
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:12,850
It's a small amount of food.

137
00:06:13,810 --> 00:06:20,310
Now for our next phrase, it's very important because I've noticed that a lot of our English learners make the mistake of using this phrase.

138
00:06:20,910 --> 00:06:21,790
It's how about.

139
00:06:22,370 --> 00:06:23,270
How about.

140
00:06:23,270 --> 00:06:29,070
So in today's dialogue, the phrase is, how about we go home and prepare a couple of sandwiches?

141
00:06:29,590 --> 00:06:37,330
So how about is used as a suggestion is, how do you feel or what do you think of going home and preparing a couple of sandwiches?

142
00:06:37,490 --> 00:06:41,310
So another way to say this is, why don't we go home and prepare some sandwiches?

143
00:06:41,570 --> 00:06:41,770
Exactly.

144
00:06:42,770 --> 00:06:51,230
But commonly, English learners make the mistake of using how about as a way of saying how was it or how is it.

145
00:06:51,470 --> 00:06:53,450
So for example, how about your weekend?

146
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:54,840
Wrong.

147
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:55,700
Okay.

148
00:06:56,060 --> 00:06:57,400
So how was your weekend?

149
00:06:57,780 --> 00:06:58,000
Exactly.

150
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:03,640
So how about is usually used when we make a suggestion.

151
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:07,000
How about we go see a movie on Saturday?

152
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,680
Or how about we go to my parents' house for Christmas this year?

153
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:17,610
Or finally, how about you get another job so that we can have more money to spend on going out to eat?

154
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:18,430
Very good.

155
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,110
So how about, these are all suggestions.

156
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:22,080
Why don't you get another job?

157
00:07:22,080 --> 00:07:24,530
Why don't we go to our parents' house for Christmas?

158
00:07:25,310 --> 00:07:28,790
So you can't say, how about your weekend?

159
00:07:29,250 --> 00:07:30,490
You say, how was your weekend?

160
00:07:30,910 --> 00:07:32,030
So there's a big difference there.

161
00:07:32,190 --> 00:07:32,570
Very good.

162
00:07:32,770 --> 00:07:36,170
So make sure to stay away from that typical mistake using how about.

163
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:42,080
